# Codon sync_timedb parse contract

**Activation:** `alwaysApply: false` — when triggers in `agent-discipline-core.mdc` match, **Read this file before editing**. Triggered rules are mandatory, not optional.

## Scope

Codon compiles the **parse+collapse numeric hot path** only (`IncrementalStatsParser` feed + plain-host / Codon-NumPy collapse). Django ORM/COPY, queue orchestrator, tar/zstd archive, and job store stay on **`/opt/python3.14t`** (`python-image-interpreter-contract.mdc`). Do **not** claim whole-daemon Codon.

## Laws

1. **Codon-NumPy** — hot path uses native `import numpy` in Codon. Forbidden: `from python import numpy` / `from python import pandas` on that path.
2. **Clang shim** — Codon still execs argv `g++`; PATH-shim to `clang++` in container builds (no apt `g++` required).
3. **pyext link + ABI + concurrent Codon workers** — Ship FT-safe module **only** via Dockerfile **`codon-build`** stage (`hpcperfstats/dbload/codon/build_codon_ext.sh` in-image; rebuild with `./scripts/rebuild_pipeline.sh`): Codon `--lib` kernel (`feed_collapse_capi.py` `@export` C entry with **per-slot cache banks**, zlib-ng on `LIBRARY_PATH`) plus `pyext_ft_init.c` multi-phase init with **`Py_MOD_GIL_NOT_USED`**, linked with `-Wl,-rpath,$ORIGIN` so `hpcperfstats_codon_parse.so`, sibling `libhpcperfstats_codon_kernel.so`, and bundled Codon runtime (`libcodonrt.so`, `libomp.so`, and Codon `libgfortran`/`libquadmath`/`libgcc_s` as needed) load from the same directory. Hard-require **`codon_pyext_314t=pass`** and **`codon_pyext_314t_gil_off=pass`** under FT with **no** `/opt/codon` on `LD_LIBRARY_PATH` (empty + E6 fingerprint + **`parse_stats_lines_codon`**; process GIL remains off after import). Bridge width **`N = max(1, round(parse_pool × sync_codon_context_pool_fraction))`** (fraction default **0.5** → N=32 at parse width 64, cap 32). Production FT + baked `.so` runs Codon in **Popen stdio workers** of size ``N`` (one codonrt per OS process via `codon_process_worker.py`; kill-only atexit — no multiprocessing teardown under FT) because codonrt is not safe across threads in one process; host unit fakes / `HPCPERFSTATS_CODON_PARSE_MODULE` stay in-process with per-slot locks. **IPC:** length-prefixed binary frames (version byte + kind/status + nbytes + payload) — request body is raw UTF-8 lines (`\\n`-joined); fingerprint response is `struct "!iidd"`; parse response is compact UTF-8 **JSON**. **Forbidden:** pickle stdio IPC; **msgpack** (C extension re-enables process GIL on 3.14t → Codon fail-closed). **Streaming divert:** `parse_stats_file_streaming_incremental` flush windows call `try_codon_feed_batch_parse` (schema-inclusive) when `emission_start==0` and no exclude list; fail-closed to `IncrementalStatsParser`. Claiming a full-load Codon win requires loaded48 Arm B / Arm A `mean_files_per_s` **≥ 2.0** with `codon_slot_occ` held>0 on Arm B. Census exposes **`codon_slot_occ=held/N`**. No process-wide codonrt serialize. Pyext must **own** UTF-8 copies into Codon (no borrowed `PyUnicode_AsUTF8` pointers). Fingerprint and parse C ABI take a **slot** argument. loaded48/Codon soaks must run the supervisor in a **subprocess** (parent pytest must not import ``hpcperfstats_codon_parse``); child kill-only Codon workers then ``os._exit`` after drain. Concurrent I/O stress must log **`codonrt_serialize=0`** and **`slot_occ_max>1`** (`test_runs/codon_stripe_stress_*.log`). Fail-closed on stress failure = **disable Codon divert** (CPython), never re-bolt process-wide serialize. Bridge **self-wires** `/opt/hpcperfstats/codon_parse` onto `sys.path` when that directory exists and sets **`OMP_NUM_THREADS=1`** before Codon import (nested libomp). Startup must log greppable **`codon_parse status=enabled|disabled`** including **`gil=off`**, **`contexts=N`**, **`codon_mode=process_pool|in_process`**, and **`codonrt_serialize=0`** when enabled. Forbidden: `Py_MOD_GIL_USED`; `PYTHON_GIL=0` as the prod “fix”; process-wide codonrt serialize as production default; claiming concurrency without a green concurrent I/O stress log (`slot_occ_max>1`); host-side prebuild / `codon_parse_image` staging / `build_codon_ext_in_pipeline.sh`; stock Codon `--pyext` `PyInit`/`from_python` on pipeline `PYTHONPATH`. Fail closed to CPython if pyext/kernel/runtime `.so` files are missing, unloadable, fingerprint/API mismatches, or GIL is enabled after Codon import.
4. **Class-free pyext compile unit** — `hpcperfstats/dbload/codon/feed_collapse.py` must contain **no** Codon/`Python` `class` definitions in the export realization graph. Use module-level constants (e.g. `HOST_PROC_KEYS`), tuples/lists/dicts of primitives, and free functions. Forbidden: nesting the kernel inside the exported fn (nested `HOST_PROC_KEYS` capture fails Codon 0.20.4 pyext). Exported APIs return only primitives or lists/dicts of primitives.
5. **Inventory** — changes that expand Codon surface must refresh `test_runs/codon_sync_timedb_inventory_*.log` (every `sync_timedb*.py` build attempt). Extra Codon units (e.g. `collapse_sum_kernel.py`) count toward maximize-surface; do not rewrite Django/orchestrator modules. Path segment `codon/` is out of scope for `scripts/python_def_inventory.py` (`excluded_reason=codon_compile_unit`); Codon dialect (`@export` / `Ptr`) is not the CPython docstring gate.
6. **A/B baseline** — Arm A = 3.14t production `IncrementalStatsParser` + `_collapse_stats_with_deltas`; Arm B = Codon feed+collapse (prefer pyext import when `.so` present; else `codon run`); same corpus/reps/warmup; log `test_runs/codon_ab_*.log` with `arm_a_elapsed_s`, `arm_b_elapsed_s`, `ratio_a_over_b`, `gate_1p25x`. Pass requires **`gate_1p25x=True`** (≥1.25×). Anti-patterns: host GIL `.venv` as Arm A; Codon vs simplified feed kernel alone; claiming win without logged Arm A. CI on a weaker host understates Granite Rapids prod speedup.
7. **GPU / `j:` stamps** — Codon feed must match `_shared_row_dev` (GPU keeps hardware `dev`; shared-node non-GPU and `host_mem_job` stamp `j:<jid>`). Collapse vectorization laws in `sync-timedb-parsing-collapse-vectorization.mdc` still apply on the CPython collapse path after Codon `finish()`-shaped parse.
8. **Native CPU + ThinLTO bake** — Every production `codon build -release` (Dockerfile `codon-build`) must pass **`--mcpu=native`** and **`--linker-flags "-flto=thin"`** (never `--disable-native`). Align `pyext_ft_init.c` compile/link with `-march=native -mtune=native -flto=thin`. Build images on the prod host (Granite Rapids); do not ship a weak-CI prebuilt as the prod artifact. Log `target-cpu` / SIMD samples in the build log.

